WEBVTT

NOTE Cues sit near the top (line:4%) so they don't cover on-screen labels.

1a-1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.870 line:4% align:center
Every MOSAIC score can be followed from start to finish.

1b-1
00:00:04.220 --> 00:00:05.820 line:4% align:center
Let’s follow one answer.

1c-1
00:00:06.700 --> 00:00:09.060 line:4% align:center
MOSAIC uses three layers of weighting.

1d-1
00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:12.143 line:4% align:center
First: how strongly a topic is represented in

1d-2
00:00:12.143 --> 00:00:13.470 line:4% align:center
the source documents.

1e-1
00:00:13.460 --> 00:00:16.533 line:4% align:center
Second: how relevant that question is to this

1e-2
00:00:16.533 --> 00:00:17.830 line:4% align:center
business’s context.

1f-1
00:00:18.140 --> 00:00:20.748 line:4% align:center
Third: how much its category contributes to the

1f-2
00:00:20.748 --> 00:00:22.580 line:4% align:center
overall result for this industry.

1g-1
00:00:23.180 --> 00:00:25.227 line:4% align:center
The system sets all three from its

1g-2
00:00:25.227 --> 00:00:26.070 line:4% align:center
configuration.

2a-1
00:00:26.810 --> 00:00:29.290 line:4% align:center
Take a fictional food business in Peru.

2b-1
00:00:30.250 --> 00:00:32.870 line:4% align:center
It’s asked: What percentage of your waste is

2b-2
00:00:32.870 --> 00:00:34.240 line:4% align:center
diverted from landfill?

2c-1
00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:36.320 line:4% align:center
The answer is fifty percent.

3a-1
00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:40.055 line:4% align:center
First, the answer becomes credit, from zero to

3a-2
00:00:40.055 --> 00:00:43.560 line:4% align:center
one hundred. Here, fifty percent becomes fifty points.

3b-1
00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:46.574 line:4% align:center
Other numerical questions use their configured

3b-2
00:00:46.574 --> 00:00:49.279 line:4% align:center
benchmarks; choice questions use predefined

3b-3
00:00:49.279 --> 00:00:50.160 line:4% align:center
answer scales.

4a-1
00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:53.795 line:4% align:center
Layer one, the base weight, is four point oh

4a-2
00:00:53.795 --> 00:00:56.975 line:4% align:center
eight: set by how widely and how often the topic

4a-3
00:00:56.975 --> 00:00:59.360 line:4% align:center
appears across the source documents.

4b-1
00:01:00.010 --> 00:01:03.212 line:4% align:center
Layer two, the context multiplier, comes from

4b-2
00:01:03.212 --> 00:01:06.130 line:4% align:center
rules that match the business’s industry,

4b-3
00:01:06.130 --> 00:01:07.980 line:4% align:center
markets, buyers and goals.

4c-1
00:01:08.240 --> 00:01:11.062 line:4% align:center
In this example, the applicable context

4c-2
00:01:11.062 --> 00:01:13.450 line:4% align:center
multiplier is one point one five.

4d-1
00:01:13.620 --> 00:01:16.441 line:4% align:center
The current configured rules increase importance

4d-2
00:01:16.441 --> 00:01:17.440 line:4% align:center
where they apply.

5a-1
00:01:18.470 --> 00:01:20.800 line:4% align:center
Credit times the adjusted weight gives two

5a-2
00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:23.462 line:4% align:center
hundred and thirty-four point six points, out of

5a-3
00:01:23.462 --> 00:01:26.180 line:4% align:center
a possible four hundred and sixty-nine point two.

5b-1
00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:29.817 line:4% align:center
A question left blank drops out of the possible

5b-2
00:01:29.817 --> 00:01:32.250 line:4% align:center
total, rather than counting as zero.

6a-1
00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:35.715 line:4% align:center
Within each category, earned points are divided

6a-2
00:01:35.715 --> 00:01:38.200 line:4% align:center
by possible points to produce its percentage.

6b-1
00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:41.879 line:4% align:center
Adding earned points across all categories, then

6b-2
00:01:41.879 --> 00:01:44.781 line:4% align:center
dividing by their combined possible points,

6b-3
00:01:44.781 --> 00:01:46.670 line:4% align:center
gives the raw overall score.

6c-1
00:01:47.210 --> 00:01:49.758 line:4% align:center
The first two layers shape both this raw score

6c-2
00:01:49.758 --> 00:01:51.530 line:4% align:center
and the industry-weighted score.

7a-1
00:01:52.350 --> 00:01:55.266 line:4% align:center
Layer three, the category weight, applies after

7a-2
00:01:55.266 --> 00:01:57.996 line:4% align:center
the category percentages are calculated, and

7a-3
00:01:57.996 --> 00:02:00.230 line:4% align:center
only to the industry-weighted score.

7b-1
00:02:00.570 --> 00:02:03.666 line:4% align:center
For food and agro-processing, Resources carries

7b-2
00:02:03.666 --> 00:02:06.565 line:4% align:center
approximately forty-nine percent, Governance

7b-3
00:02:06.565 --> 00:02:09.990 line:4% align:center
thirty-one, and People and Community about ten each.

7c-1
00:02:10.260 --> 00:02:12.512 line:4% align:center
Multiplied and added together, they give the

7c-2
00:02:12.512 --> 00:02:13.740 line:4% align:center
industry-weighted score.

8a-1
00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:16.823 line:4% align:center
Under the same configuration and business

8a-2
00:02:16.823 --> 00:02:19.430 line:4% align:center
context, the same answers always give the same

8a-3
00:02:19.430 --> 00:02:20.450 line:4% align:center
calculated scores.

9a-1
00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:24.430 line:4% align:center
MOSAIC. The pieces that matter.
